# Trimmed from MD/finite_temperature/uq/lammps_inputs/in.matensemble for the
# coordination-stability check (confirmed 2026-09): that recipe's own NVT
# melt (4500K) / anneal stages are for a different, structure-diversity-
# generation purpose and were never actually needed here -- cn_checker.py's
# own default check_file (data.npt_relax) is written right after the
# room-temperature NPT stage below, before melt/anneal would even start, so
# running them would only add ~2/3 more compute per structure for no effect
# on this check. Everything else (variable names read by
# lammps_reaxff_md.py, dump/pair_style setup, minimize stages) is otherwise
# unchanged from in.matensemble.
#
# pair_style/fix below use the /kk (Kokkos GPU) suffix (confirmed 2026-09:
# every run up to this point used the plain, unsuffixed CPU-only reaxff/
# qeq/reax -- one core, GPU idle despite gpus_per_task=1 being reserved per
# chore -- this is the fix). Requires lammps_reaxff_md.py's own
# cmdargs=[..., "-k","on","g","1","-sf","kk",...] (see that driver's own
# docstring) -- "-sf kk" alone would have auto-suffixed these anyway, but
# spelling it out here keeps the intent visible in the one file that
# actually defines the physics, rather than relying purely on an implicit
# command-line flag elsewhere.

# VARIABLES
variable        T_room                  equal 300

# run length -- <=10ps at timestep 0.5fs per the user's own sizing (2026-09)
variable room_steps     equal 20000

units real
dimension 3
boundary p p p
atom_style charge
box tilt large
processors * * *
# KOKKOS's own GPU default is "neigh full" + "newton off" (confirmed via
# source, 2026-09, src/KOKKOS/kokkos.cpp: ngpus>0 -> neighflag=FULL,
# newtonflag=0) -- but pair_style reaxff/kk's init_style() calls straight
# through to the BASE (non-Kokkos) PairReaxFF::init_style()
# (src/KOKKOS/pair_reaxff_kokkos.cpp:168), which unconditionally requires
# newton pair ON (src/REAXFF/pair_reaxff.cpp:364) -- this is a genuine
# conflict with Kokkos's own GPU default, NOT a sign that ReaxFF can't run
# on GPU at all. pair_reaxff_kokkos.cpp's own force loops explicitly
# branch on HALF/HALFTHREAD/FULL (confirmed by reading its source), so it
# supports a half neighbor list too -- the fix is to override Kokkos's
# default via `package kokkos neigh half`, which the same source
# (kokkos.cpp's accelerator() parsing) confirms auto-promotes to the
# GPU-safe HALFTHREAD variant whenever ngpus>0, rather than switching off
# GPU use entirely.
package kokkos neigh half neigh/qeq half newton on
newton on
neighbor 3.0 bin
neigh_modify every 1 delay 0 check yes

read_data ${structure}

pair_style reaxff/kk ${control_filename} safezone 3.0 mincap 500
pair_coeff * * ${ff_filename} ${elements}

fix 1 all qeq/reax/kk 1 0.0 10.0 1.0e-6 reaxff

thermo 		1000
thermo_style 	custom step temp pe epair etotal press pxx pyy pzz lx ly lz vol density

dump            d1 all custom 1000 ${dump_file} id type x y z fx fy fz
dump_modify     d1 element ${elements}
# ${dump_file} (set by lammps_reaxff_md.py) has no "*" wildcard, so every
# snapshot appends to this one file rather than LAMMPS writing a separate
# dump_<timestep>.dump per snapshot -- see that driver's own docstring for
# why (HPC scratch filesystems' total-file-count quotas). sort id belongs
# here (not left to the reader) so the file itself is already atom-id
# ordered at the source, matching the reader's own order=True default.
dump_modify     d1 sort id

timestep        0.5

#------------------- ENERGY_MINIMIZATION ---------------------
# Both stages use cg/kk, not fire -- CONFIRMED (2026-09, via the actual
# error: "Must use a Kokkos-enabled min style ... with Kokkos minimize"):
# this build has no fire/kk (only cg/kk among Kokkos-enabled minimizers),
# and Kokkos requires every min_style actually used to be Kokkos-enabled
# -- unlike pair_style/fix's auto-suffix, there's no silent CPU fallback
# for minimize (atoms/data live in Kokkos's own memory space; falling
# back to a CPU-only minimizer mid-run isn't something LAMMPS does
# quietly). Loose/tight distinction kept via minimize's own tolerance
# args, not via a different min_style for stage 1.
# stage 1: fast, loose (get rid of large forces)
min_style cg/kk
minimize 1.0e-2 1.0e-2 500 5000

# stage 2: tighter refine
min_style cg/kk
minimize 1.0e-6 1.0e-4 2000 10000
# ${output_dir} (set by lammps_reaxff_md.py, same convention as
# ${dump_file}) -- CONFIRMED necessary, not cosmetic (2026-09): a bare
# relative filename here writes into this chore's own process CWD, not
# this structure's own output directory, and gets silently overwritten by
# every other structure this same chore processes afterward. See that
# driver's own comment on ${output_dir} for how this was actually caught.
write_data      ${output_dir}/Min.data

#------------------- NPT AT ${T_room} ------------------------
# data.npt_relax below is what cn_checker.py compares against the pre-MD
# structure.lmp -- see this file's own header comment.
fix             relax all npt temp ${T_room} ${T_room} 100 x 0 0 100 y 0 0 100
run             ${room_steps}
unfix           relax
write_restart   ${output_dir}/npt_relax.res
write_data      ${output_dir}/data.npt_relax
